      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/lQ1CJb3aQqhyuL95_t32-3ygMWI=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/AR-216759-The-Perfect-Cinnamon-Roll-Icing-DDMFS-Step-04-4fb46256c13e4ca2b656573999653a1b.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/216759/step_04.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Frost the cinnamon rolls with about ¼ of the icing when they are still warm. When they’re cooled, top with remaining icing. The bottom layer will not only melt into the pastry, it will serve as a sort of protective barrier that will keep the cinnamon rolls fresher for longer. Enjoy!",
